# Data is never committed (SPEC §1). Point config paths at ~/subneptune_data,
# or create a convenience symlink `data -> ~/subneptune_data`.
# Ignore the contents, not the directory: git will not descend into an excluded
# directory, so `/data/` would make the negation below unreachable.
/data/*
# ...except the released data products, which are outputs of this code rather
# than the raw inputs SPEC §1 keeps out (A70).
!/data/release/

# Run outputs (structure profiles, figures rendered to disk, cached tables)
/outputs/
*.npz
*.png
*.pdf
!docs/**/*.png
# The ARC pull is provenance for the Extended Data: its figures are part of
# the record, so the PNG rule above is lifted inside it.
!ed_data/**/*.png
# A78's bundle carries the production dipole series and the spectra they
# produce. These are inputs to a gate, not run outputs, so the *.npz rule is
# lifted inside the pull too (A78).
!ed_data/**/*.npz
# ...but A80's dipole bundle is 41 MB of raw trajectory product across 67 cells,
# which is exactly the raw input SPEC §1 keeps out of the repo. It stays on
# disk beside the other data; the A80 gates read it the same way every opacity
# gate reads ~/subneptune_data, and skip cleanly when it is absent (A80).
ed_data/arc_dipoles/
# A78's five cells (dipole series + the delivered v3 spectrum it reproduces)
# are the same kind of raw production output; not committed since the move
# into water-scw-mace, fingerprinted in ed_data/arc_a78_dipoles_sha256.json.
ed_data/arc_a78/T*/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# OS
.DS_Store
figs_v3/
data_release_v3/
outputs_v3/
